 "intro": "Before Tigranocerta, the new capital of Armenia, 6 October 69 BC. King Tigranes the Great comes with an enormous army to relieve the city. You are Lucius Licinius Lucullus, with perhaps 10,000 foot and 1,000 horse.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s account, Tigranes mocked the small Roman army as too many for envoys and too few for soldiers. Lucullus, told the day was unlucky, said he would make it lucky. He led two cohorts up a slope to attack the Armenian cataphracts on a hill, telling his men to strike at their legs; the cataphracts panicked and fled back into their own army, which broke. The Romans claimed huge enemy losses. The city’s mercenaries opened its gates. The other choices are what-ifs.",
